# 2️⃣ EXISTS vs IN

Very important interview topic.

---

# 🔹 IN

Checks if value exists in a list/result.

---

## Example

```sql id="3m5ycg"
SELECT name
FROM students
WHERE id IN
(
 SELECT student_id
 FROM enrollments
);
```

---

## Mental Model

```text id="6mgoz9"
IN = “Is value inside this set?”
```

---

# 🔹 EXISTS

Checks whether subquery returns ANY row.

---

## Example

```sql id="i9wr8i"
SELECT name
FROM students s
WHERE EXISTS
(
 SELECT 1
 FROM enrollments e
 WHERE s.id = e.student_id
);
```

---

# Mental Model

```text id="i0ibz6"
EXISTS = “Does matching row exist?”
```

---

# Key Difference

---

## IN

Database first creates whole result set.

Then compares.

---

## EXISTS

Stops immediately once match found.

Usually faster for large datasets.

---

# Easy Comparison

| Feature     | IN            | EXISTS                  |
| ----------- | ------------- | ----------------------- |
| Works on    | Values        | Rows                    |
| Good for    | Small sets    | Large correlated checks |
| Performance | Can be slower | Often faster            |

---

# Python Analogy 🧠

## IN

```python id="6j8owg"
if student_id in valid_ids:
```

---

## EXISTS

```python id="g11d8s"
found = False

for e in enrollments:
    if e["student_id"] == s["id"]:
        found = True
        break
```

Stops early.

---

# When EXISTS Shines

Very useful when:

* Checking relationships
* Large tables
* Correlated subqueries

---

# Memory Tricks 🧠

```text id="r0ajkl"
IN → compare values

EXISTS → check row existence
```

